reason=Incident label events reconcile CI mode. New .github/workflows/incident-label-ci.yml (134 lines) acts on a labeled/unlabeled event for expedited-incident-response ONLY, on a same-repo PR. It selects the newest pull_request ci.yml run of that PR (by number) on its current head; with none listed yet it stops green. Otherwise it at once creates an in-progress ci-green check run (a hold) as the GitHub Actions app, whose ci-green the merge ruleset requires, so nothing merges on the stale verdict, including after a COMPLETED expedited run. It then makes the CI run's own newest ci-green non-success: an unfinished run is cancelled, and a completed run is re-run and that attempt cancelled, so ci-green, which runs if: always(), concludes failure. It verifies that, releases the hold as neutral (a hold left open would block the head forever, as measured), and re-runs; the re-run's ci-green decides. Its concurrency group is shared only by incident label events. auto-enable-merge.yml gains one gate conjunct plus 4 comment lines, inserted with no existing line changed: it skips the unlabeled event of that label, so it cannot race the hold. That only narrows when auto-merge arms. Any other label skips the new job at the job level (no runner), and ci.yml's triggers are unchanged; an incident label event costs one short ubuntu-latest job, one immediately cancelled attempt and one CI re-run. 139 lines added, 0 removed or modified against merge base 356b21ae; no check removed; the required-check set unchanged. The reusable-check-matrix omission half was split out to livespec-dev-tooling-hlxbsv: it reduces a quality gate (maintainer tier).
